    "case_summary": "A woman in her 50s with morbid obesity and obstructive sleep apnea presented with 3 days of fever with a temperature up to 39°C, anosmia, and shortness of breath. Medical history significant for morbid obesity and obstructive sleep apnea.\n\nOxygen saturation of 85% on room air and coarse rales at the lung bases bilaterally.\n\n- Laboratory Tests: Nasopharyngeal swab positive by reverse transcriptase–polymerase chain reaction.- Imaging Studies:  - Chest Radiography: Suggestive of bilateral multifocal pneumonia  - ECG Studies:  Title: Figure 1A - ECG in prone position  Description: Normal sinus rhythm with normal frontal QRS axis. Precordial leads showed low amplitudes and Q waves in leads V1 to V3    Title: Figure 1B - ECG in supine position   Description: Normal ECG findings\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?\n\nOptions:\nA. Coronavirus Disease 2019 (COVID-19) with Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome (ARDS)\nB. COVID-19 pneumonia\nC. Acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS)\nD. Acute hypoxemic respiratory failure\n",
